		{
			"outputs":[
				
			],
			"color":"#234",
			"widgets_values":[
				"# Akatz Labs · Character Swap LoRA v1\n\n## 1. Download the character LoRA\n[Model card](https://huggingface.co/akatz-ai/MiniMax-H3-Character-Swap-LoRA) · [Download the 1000-step weights](https://huggingface.co/akatz-ai/MiniMax-H3-Character-Swap-LoRA/resolve/main/h3_character_swap_pro4500_1000.safetensors)\n\nPut `h3_character_swap_pro4500_1000.safetensors` in **ComfyUI/models/loras/** and refresh the model list (or restart ComfyUI). Select it in **Load LoRA** node, with **strength 1.0**. Set strength to 0 for a base-model comparison. No trigger word is needed.\n\n## 2. Supply your inputs\n- Upload a replacement image or character sheet into **<Picture 1>**.\n- Upload a short **24 fps** source clip into **<Video 1>**. Start with a continuous shot around 5 seconds.\n- Edit the prompt to identify exactly who to replace. The reference supplies identity, outfit and art style; the video supplies performance and scene.\n- The loader does **not** resample frame rate. Convert non-24-fps clips beforehand while preserving playback speed.\n\n## 3. Default settings\n**Ref2VA INT8 · character LoRA 1.0 · 20 steps · res_multistep / simple · Turbo OFF.** All execution nodes are built into ComfyUI; no custom-node pack is required. Validated against ComfyUI 0.37.0.\n\nThe optional Turbo branch is preserved from the official template. Its loader is **bypassed** so its weights are not required. To enable Turbo: download its listed weights, select its loader and press **Ctrl+B** to un-bypass it, then turn **Enable optional Turbo** on. This is a separate accelerator; the character LoRA remains active with either branch.\n\nResolution starts at **0.4 MP / 864 × 480**. Set **0.98 MP / 1344 × 768** for 768p; match the source aspect ratio. Higher resolution, longer clips and larger references require more memory. This is not a blanket 24 GB fit guarantee.\n\nSet duration to match your clip. H3 uses **24 fps** and **17n+5 frames**: 5 seconds rounds up to **124 frames / 5.167 seconds**. For aligned comparisons, prepare a matching frame count or trim the final output.\n\n## 4. Audio and limitations\nSource audio is disconnected by default so silent clips work. If your source has sound, optionally connect **Get Video Components → audio** to **ref_video_audios.ref_video_audio_0**. H3 still generates audio; exact preservation requires muxing the original soundtrack afterward.\n\nV1 can drift in timing, facial expressions and hard cuts, especially on long clips. Source-video conditioning is not a pixel-preserving mask. Keep prompts clear; additional wording does not guarantee stronger adherence.\n\nA compatible Ref2VA hybrid can be selected in the model loader, but it is not required or bundled. Plain FL2VA/T2V weights are not a drop-in replacement for this reference workflow.\n\n## Upstream\nBased on [ComfyUI's official H3 Ref2VA template](https://github.com/Comfy-Org/workflow_templates/blob/main/templates/video_minimax_h3_r2v.json). Its original notes are retained. **Save/export this workflow after selecting your own inputs.**"
			],
